  "bookName": "Proverbs",
  "bookOrder": 20,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 1,
  "sortOrder": 20001,
  "verseCount": 33,
  "aliases": [
    "Prov",
    "Pr",
    "Prv"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "The proverbs of Solomon the son of David, king of Israel;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "To know wisdom and instruction; to perceive the words of understanding;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "To receive the instruction of wisdom, justice, and judgment, and equity;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "To give subtilty to the simple, to the young man knowledge and discretion.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "A wise man will hear, and will increase learning; and a man of understanding shall attain unto wise counsels:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "To understand a proverb, and the interpretation; the words of the wise, and their dark sayings.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge: but fools despise wisdom and instruction.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "My son, hear the instruction of thy father, and forsake not the law of thy mother:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "For they shall be an ornament of grace unto thy head, and chains about thy neck.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "My son, if sinners entice thee, consent thou not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "If they say, Come with us, let us lay wait for blood, let us lurk privily for the innocent without cause:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Let us swallow them up alive as the grave; and whole, as those that go down into the pit:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "We shall find all precious substance, we shall fill our houses with spoil:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Cast in thy lot among us; let us all have one purse:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "My son, walk not thou in the way with them; refrain thy foot from their path:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "For their feet run to evil, and make haste to shed blood.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Surely in vain the net is spread in the sight of any bird.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "And they lay wait for their own blood; they lurk privily for their own lives.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "So are the ways of every one that is greedy of gain; which taketh away the life of the owners thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Wisdom crieth without; she uttereth her voice in the streets:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "She crieth in the chief place of concourse, in the openings of the gates: in the city she uttereth her words, saying,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "How long, ye simple ones, will ye love simplicity? and the scorners delight in their scorning, and fools hate knowledge?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Turn you at my reproof: behold, I will pour out my spirit unto you, I will make known my words unto you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Because I have called, and ye refused; I have stretched out my hand, and no man regarded;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "But ye have set at nought all my counsel, and would none of my reproof:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "I also will laugh at your calamity; I will mock when your fear cometh;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "When your fear cometh as desolation, and your destruction cometh as a whirlwind; when distress and anguish cometh upon you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Then shall they call upon me, but I will not answer; they shall seek me early, but they shall not find me:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "For that they hated knowledge, and did not choose the fear of the LORD:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "They would none of my counsel: they despised all my reproof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "Therefore shall they eat of the fruit of their own way, and be filled with their own devices.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "For the turning away of the simple shall slay them, and the prosperity of fools shall destroy them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:1:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "But whoso hearkeneth unto me shall dwell safely, and shall be quiet from fear of evil.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 1:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:1:33"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
